#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:212
msgid "Recommended server configuration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:213
msgid "None of these are checked by the report below — a plugin cannot see past a reverse proxy to tell how your server is configured. They are what a host should be doing anyway."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:218
msgid "TLS 1.2 or 1.3, with TLS 1.0 and 1.1 disabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:219
msgid "the older versions are deprecated and refused outright by modern API endpoints, so a server still relying on them will see calls to Laposta fail at the handshake. They also leave your visitors negotiating cipher suites with known weaknesses — and this plugin's signup forms carry a name and an email address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:222
msgid "HTTP/2 or HTTP/3"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:223
msgid "these carry many requests over one connection instead of queueing them. It changes nothing about what this plugin does, but the settings screen and the block editor each pull a good number of small files, and on HTTP/1.1 those wait in line. General hygiene rather than a requirement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:226
msgid "A persistent object cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:227
msgid "this plugin leans on transients — for cached campaigns, for the connection verdict, for the signup rate limits. Without a persistent cache those are rows in the options table; with one they stay in memory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:230
msgid "Current versions of everything"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:231
msgid "the versions the report advises are the newest that have been out long enough to be widely deployed. Running behind them is not necessarily broken — it is untested, which is a different thing and the reason the plugin warns rather than refuses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:259
msgid "Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/AboutTab.php:263
msgid "This plugin bundles no third-party runtime dependencies. It requires only PHP and WordPress itself."
msgstr ""

